  "sourceType": "SYNTHESISED",
  "sourceNotes": "Guinness is used as a braising liquid in Irish and British cooking. It appears in Irish cookbooks from the mid-twentieth century. The combination of Guinness with beef or lamb is associated with Irish pub cooking and became part of British domestic repertoire through the cookery writing of Darina Allen and others in the 1980s and 1990s.",
