  "body": {
    "type": "doc",
    "content": [
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Beef and Guinness stew uses "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "beef shin",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termSlug": "beef-shin"
                }
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " braised in Guinness for three hours until the meat falls apart and the sauce is dark and thick. The stout gives a slight bitterness that stops the stew from being cloying. The work is mostly done by the oven; the hands-on time is under 20 minutes."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "infoPanel",
        "attrs": {
          "tone": "tip"
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Brown the beef in batches in a hot pan. Crowding the pan traps steam and makes the meat grey rather than browned. Each batch needs space and heat."
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
